menu "433MHz Receiver"

    config RX433_GPIO
        int "Receiver DATA GPIO"
        range 0 48
        default 11
        help
            GPIO connected to the 433 MHz receiver DATA output. The component
            doesn't read this itself; pass it in rx433_config_t.gpio.

    config RX433_BITS
        int "Expected bits per frame (0 = any 12-32)"
        range 0 32
        default 24
        help
            Frames with any other length are dropped. EV1527 remotes send
            24 bits; PT2262-style ones send 12 or 24 depending on how they
            are read.

    config RX433_RELEASE_MS
        int "Release timeout (ms)"
        range 50 2000
        default 400
        help
            A RELEASE event is sent when no frame of the held code has
            arrived for this long. Remotes repeat every ~40-50 ms while a
            button is held, but a weak remote near interference can drop
            frames for ~300 ms at a time; shorter than that splits one
            press into two.

    config RX433_LOG_FRAMES
        bool "Log every decoded frame"
        default n
        help
            Logs each frame before the two-identical-frames check and press
            tracking. Useful for checking a new remote decodes at all.

    config RX433_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Decoder task priority"
        range 1 24
        default 10

endmenu
